{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/361322-just-found-a-site-where-a-few-old-questions-and-answers-by-the-developers-are-listed","id":361322,"title":"just found a site where a few old questions and answers by the developers are listed.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-06T08:29:33-08:00","id":361322,"title":"just found a site where a few old questions and answers by the developers are listed.","content":"it's only a few of them and nothing really major but for anyone interested here it is<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.oocities.org/vtmfaq/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.oocities.org/vtmfaq/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.oocities.org/vtmfaq/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.oocities.org/vtmfaq/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> if anyone knows any similar site or has kept some documents in their pc of old questions and answers then please post them here if possible so we can compile them. same goes for any forum where a developer clarifies sth.<br /> <br /> oh and here's one more though it's more recent. <a href=\"http://eyebeams.livejournal.com/396330.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://eyebeams.livejournal.com/396330.html</a> it's about mage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T16:28:34-08:00","id":361703,"title":"","content":"I have some of that listed above (Malcolm's cut material from Ascension) and a bunch of other material as well. I'm not sure on the sources of some of it (it's all in one big &quot;Mage Notes&quot; doc) but some is clearly from devs. I also have a dev chat with Jesse Heinig from 20th March 2000. I'll post them over in the Mage forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T16:56:13-08:00","id":361735,"title":"","content":"Here you go:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/361711-mage-developer-chat-notes-snippets-etc-really-long\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/361711-mage-developer-chat-notes-snippets-etc-really-long\"> Mage Developer Chat, Notes, Snippets etc. REALLY LONG! - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/361711-mage-developer-chat-notes-snippets-etc-really-long\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/361711-mage-developer-chat-notes-snippets-etc-really-long </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> OK, so I've joined the trawl for bits and pieces of developer info posted over the years across the internet. And I came up with a few bits and pieces on my hard </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T17:05:20-08:00","id":361754,"title":"","content":"On a roll today <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Here's a dev chat for Mummy: the Resurrection from 21st March 2001:<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy: The Resurrection</b><br /> <i><b>The Developer Chat Transcript</b></i><br /> <br /> <br /> Welcome to the Transcript for the moderated Mummy: The Resurrection Developer's chat of March 21st, 2001, featuring Andrew Bates. The Transcript has been edited to include only those questions which Andrew had the opportunity to answer, and a few amusing comments that were made along the way.<br /> <br /> <b>Conrad Hubbard (ID=18)</b> (21-Mar-01 6:43:41 PM)<br /> (This user is now known as Moderator Conrad)<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 6:47:51 PM)<br /> HI all<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 6:47:56 PM)<br /> we are still waiting for Andrew<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 6:48:03 PM)<br /> got about 10 minutes to go<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 6:50:47 PM)<br /> he's on the West Coast<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 6:50:54 PM)<br /> I hope he figured time right<br /> <br /> <b>Bin_Bin_The_super_monkey (ID=30)</b> (21-Mar-01 6:51:06 PM)<br /> Uh oh...<br /> <br /> <b>GreyWolf (ID=25)</b> (21-Mar-01 6:51:09 PM)<br /> wouldn't that be amusing<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 6:52:45 PM)<br /> okay, he's here, folks, we will be starting in about 5 minutes<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 6:57:53 PM)<br /> Okay folks<br /> Andrew Bates came to White Wolf in 1995, long before my time here.<br /> Most of you are probably most familiar with his work pioneering the development of the popular game Trinity.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 6:59:05 PM)<br /> Most recently has has taken over development of Mummy: The Resurrection and is currently working on a series of Year of the Scarab novels.<br /> So let's give Andrew a warm welcome, and start the questions rolling...<br /> <br /> <b>ArroganceX (ID=22)</b> (21-Mar-01 6:59:40 PM)<br /> hey Andrew <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/image/png;base64,R0lGODlhGQAZAHcAMSH  ZAP ZM/ ZZv Zmf ZzP Z///MAP/MM//MZv/Mmf/MzP/M////AP//M///Zv//mf//zP///wECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwj/AAEIHChwBYAVVgwSXMjwicA8gEiRypOHoUU9VVSpcqaKmjNqo0hV0aNw4ZMqfzQ6 7hSpao8VRwu1PPH2R8rVTxWI2XlyUZnefQQXFEFkDNAETdSWypRD6mVFRVaydPyDzVAHqlp1Ih1FFArAqs8XXrVSkdqIj96XEmqIKBR1dSqerKy2k1VcdeOEgqAKku0Zpeqyrh0pTNkeRySSpX1I6msGzt TOUs5IonWP9qJsvSMMwVT/M6Ey06K VRgAz6bazV8E/DhxMDeMtaVeqegBiv9LrXoFjDa5 wWMGCLuyQBKk2M20lCaYkVh7zRlZlIFG/hp 0iTTH5 5RFYfqMqHKm2RPPdODNqyShxQyZ6RUSXQfEqZMi2K9HquMrJNIiyYBMB5FE4UHoEUJCZSgRQEBADs=\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>)<br /> <br /> <b>Mr.Poor (ID=54)</b> (21-Mar-01 6:59:42 PM)<br /> Hello, Mr.Bates.<br /> <br /> <b>Krister M. Michl (ID=44)</b> (21-Mar-01 6:59:45 PM)<br /> Good evening Andrew, and welcome to the world of breathing mortals...(hopefully)<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 6:59:53 PM)<br /> Hey everyone. Fire away.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:00:07 PM)<br /> Welcome, and thank you for your time today Mr. Bates. Your work as a developer for White Wolf has so far centered on games that involve hope and the struggle to make the world a better place as primary themes, with Trinity and now the world of Darkness' Mummy. Do you Feel you are more adept at exploring these themes than other themes, or has it been by fluke and happenstance?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:01:00 PM)<br /> Heh. Good question. I wasn't sure other people would notice I keep touching on the whole &quot;hope&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:01:57 PM)<br /> I guess I do feel more comfortable exploring such concepts -- as opposed to, say, ultimate damnation and the like. Honestly, I've never been a fan of the WoD as viewed solely as a place of depression and such.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:02:32 PM)<br /> I like to think that even in the darkest of circumstances, there's still hope, the possibility of redemption. Doesn't mean it's a foregone conclusion, by any means, but at least it's there.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:03:12 PM)<br /> So I guess it's natural that I've gravitated toward projects that focus on hope. (Though I still have fun dealing with darker themes.)<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:03:22 PM)<br /> Next?<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:03:35 PM)<br /> Do Mummy's have some form of split personality because of their dual souls or do they become a new entity<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:04:51 PM)<br /> It depends. When we worked on the game's initial design, we agreed it might be difficult for some people to get a handle on playing a millennia-old personality. So the combination of the new and old spirit portions felt, to us, to be thematically and roleplaying-wise, a good solution.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:05:27 PM)<br /> As such, it's really up to the individual player. He may choose to focus on his &quot;modern&quot; personality, or channel his &quot;ancient&quot; one as a concience/sporadic voice/whatever.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:06:32 PM)<br /> For instance, the main mummy character in the Scarab trilogy I'm writing is, for the most part, a very modern personality. His tem-akh pops up every so often, usally emerging in times of stress.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:06:57 PM)<br /> I think it makes it more dramatic that way, but also it helps the reader identify with him while still conveying his supernatural nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:07:25 PM)<br /> what started the &quot;rebirth&quot; of the mummies. i was under the understanding that the rite was lost<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:08:08 PM)<br /> To get the full context, it helps to know a little about other WoD games (notably Wraith).<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:09:03 PM)<br /> A few years back there was the Sixth Great Maelstrom, a huge storm that ripped through the underworld. Simply put, this storm roused Osiris from slumber (he'd been in the shadowlands for a looooong time), and sent him across the Shroud separating the spirit and physical worlds.<br /> <br /> <b>osiris (ID=55)</b> (21-Mar-01 7:09:39 PM)<br /> me!<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:10:06 PM)<br /> Except he's not truly back, completely. He needed his minions, those loyal mummies. Except there weren't that many and the Spell of Life was lost. Osiris had spent part of his centuries dozing working out what'd been wrong with the first Spell, though, and so bestowed his followers with a brand-new Spell of Life.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:10:10 PM)<br /> Viola! New mummies.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:10:36 PM)<br /> Okay we lost Andrew folks<br /> <br /> <b>Traelik'han (ID=28)</b> (21-Mar-01 7:10:39 PM)<br /> Oh no<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:10:42 PM)<br /> let's wait for him to log back in<br /> <br /> <b>SatanJr (ID=66)</b> (21-Mar-01 7:10:42 PM)<br /> DARN!<br /> <br /> <b>One1r0mancer (ID=32)</b> (21-Mar-01 7:10:46 PM)<br /> NOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO!!!!!!!!!<br /> <br /> <b>Lono (ID=19)</b> (21-Mar-01 7:10:58 PM)<br /> I think Osiris cursed him for spilling the beans on his secret. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/image/png;base64,R0lGODlhGQAZAHcAMSH  ZAP ZM/ ZZv Zmf ZzP Z///MAP/MM//MZv/Mmf/MzP/M////AP//M///Zv//mf//zP///wECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwj/AAEIHChwBYAVVgwSXMjwicA8gEiRypOHoUU9VSQ6U0XNmbNRpKroUbjwSZU8HqmpdNax48QqDhfq \" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>osiris (ID=55)</b> (21-Mar-01 7:11:09 PM)<br /> i did not!<br /> <br /> <b>Traelik'han (ID=28)</b> (21-Mar-01 7:11:09 PM)<br /> **performs the spell of life on Andrew's computer**<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:11:21 PM)<br /> Um, ow.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:11:26 PM)<br /> Okay, he's back<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:11:30 PM)<br /> let's get the next question<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:11:38 PM)<br /> Where does Horus play into all of this?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:12:15 PM)<br /> Horus has a more active role in the WoD nowadays, but exactly what that is is left a bit open.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:12:40 PM)<br /> Ostensibly, he's Osiris go-to guy, the top mummy, the big man, gathering his legions to kick ass against Set and the rest.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:13:42 PM)<br /> There are rumors, though, that Horus is feeling he'd rather Osiris stayed out of things, and that Horus should be the only Living God in the mix. (Said rumors leave it up to individuals as to whether they want an internal struggle.)<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:14:28 PM)<br /> What kind of supplements do you have in mind after the Year of the Scarab?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:15:43 PM)<br /> That's not my call, actually (and maybe Conrad can list what's on the schedule). The other YotS books were determined by the respective line authors, and I, um, don't know what they picked. The only thing I had a say in is the Scarab fiction trilogy I'm writing.<br /> I think Vampire plans Cairo by Night, Werewolf a Rage Across Egypt, Hunter a book on Middle Eastern hunters, Mage something on the Al-i-Batan and, um, those other mages.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:16:18 PM)<br /> So far folks the planned Year of the Scarab books are all listed on the Mummy web page if Andrew doesn't know of any other secret ones.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:16:46 PM)<br /> What is the trilogy about, in short?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:17:00 PM)<br /> In short: mummies!<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:17:05 PM)<br /> (Okay, in longer...)<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:17:38 PM)<br /> Will the trilogy feature a character based on The Rock?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:18:19 PM)<br /> It's about a group of hunters who stumble across an ancient artifact hidden in Chicago, of all places, and get wrapped up in a struggle with supernatural forces including mummies, vampires, and one very stubborn risen.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:19:06 PM)<br /> (Said artifact may, or may not be, a portion of Osiris' long-lost body. The struggle may have something to do with the new Spell of Life, too, and what it means to supernaturals other than mummies.)<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:19:25 PM)<br /> Okay, no &quot;may&quot; about it. But you'll have to read 'em to find out just what.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:19:41 PM)<br /> Do the Children of Osiris (the vampire bloodline) know about the new mummies, and are they going to be involved in the fight?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:20:37 PM)<br /> In fact, the Children of Osiris have somehow been cured of their curse by Osiris himself. Human once again, they serve the new mummies loyally (some say, too loyally).<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:21:10 PM)<br /> (No one knows how Osiris cured them, but certain vampires sure would like to know the trick...)<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:21:52 PM)<br /> Basically My Question is Two Forked .. . and Both Deal with Cross-Over (sorry), Are Mummy's of the Weaver or the Wyld? For the Werewolves, and are Mummy's &quot;Monsters&quot; In dealing with Hunters? Or is it more like a Mage type Circumstance of Hunters being Indifferent to them?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:22:36 PM)<br /> Well, before doing the crossover angle, bear this in mind: Before everything else, mummies are agents of Balance.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:22:49 PM)<br /> Everything they do is (supposed to be) motivated by that fact.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:23:27 PM)<br /> I'm less savvy on Werewolf, but I'd say that'd tend to place them in the Weaver camp.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:24:03 PM)<br /> Hunters are divided in their opinions. They are, ostensibly, supernaturals, which they're sworn to battle. But the mummies seem to be fighting many of the same foes as hunters do.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b><br /> are there any 'new' bane mummies?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:25:10 PM)<br /> There aren't any more of the signature Bane mummies; still the same old crew. But they're doing their best to churn out their own shock troops - Asekh-sen<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:25:59 PM)<br /> Then there's the human cult of The Amkhat, who're freaky mummy cannibal-types.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:27:10 PM)<br /> Is there much inter-conflict between the varying mummy types???<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:27:47 PM)<br /> They get along all right overall (being united in restoring the natural balance to the universe and all), but they definitely have conflicts.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:28:08 PM)<br /> The main thing is that the different Amenti (mummy types) have different ideas on how to do the job.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:29:27 PM)<br /> Plus, there are groups like the Children of Osiris, Cult of Isis, Shemsu-Heru, and the Eset-a. These are the cults/groups/followers associated with mummies, and each has its own idea on what to do.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:30:18 PM)<br /> So while there's no outright fighting among mummies (yet, anyway), there are definitely squabbles and the occasional skirmish. Your regular dysfunctional WoD family.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:30:34 PM)<br /> are there any info on the good old bane mummies in the new book or do I have get the old one?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:31:09 PM)<br /> Mummy: The Resurrection is designed to supercede previous editions of Mummy. Nothing saying you can't use the old books, but this is all fresh and tasty.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:31:48 PM)<br /> That includes the Bane mummies. They have been somewhat changed by recent circumstances (though not as much as regular mummies have been). So they get new write-ups and updated power descriptions.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:32:16 PM)<br /> Plus there's extensive words on their minions the Reapers (Asekh-sen), and enemy groups like the Amkhat.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:32:31 PM)<br /> Is M:tR destined to become a supported &quot;sub-line&quot;, like KotE?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:33:09 PM)<br /> Depends on how it sells, really. If it proves as popular as KotE did, then I'm sure White Wolf would be happy to expand Mummy into its own sub-line.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:33:48 PM)<br /> Remember that KotE, when it first came out, wasn't intended as a sub-line. We just thought it'd be a fantastic book. Fan response was so strong, though, that we were happy to provide further supplements.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:34:20 PM)<br /> The same deal goes for Mummy. As it is, I'm really happy with it and think fans will enjoy the hell out of it. If that means it sells well enough to call for further supplements, even better!<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:34:48 PM)<br /> (Aside from the already planned YotS books, of course.)<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:34:53 PM)<br /> Silly question, but is kemintiri still arround, and any idea what her reaction too all these new mummies, plus the recent Children of Osiris stuff?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:36:21 PM)<br /> She's not specifically mentioned in Mummy, so unless there's word in, say, Cairo by Night, she's still around.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:36:55 PM)<br /> Far as her reaction goes, that's really up to you. However, I'd say it'd be along the lines of many other vampires' reactions: Just how the hell did they do that?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:37:14 PM)<br /> (I imagine she's at least as interested in what makes the new breed of mummies tick, to boot.)<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:37:46 PM)<br /> What prompted White Wolf to come out with a new Mummy?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:38:03 PM)<br /> Hmmm; good question. Let me see if I can remember.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:38:17 PM)<br /> A couple different factors, I think.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:39:03 PM)<br /> Part was that WW needed a new &quot;Year of&quot; theme. We saw how successful the East was, and there was a general consensus that it'd be nice to check out other relatively-unexplored portions of the WoD.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:39:46 PM)<br /> A lot of folks (myself included) felt there was a lot more we could do with mummies than had been handled in the previous versions of the book, so why not build on that?<br /> So that's what we did. The whole Year of the Scarab theme gave us all the same opportunities to break new ground that the Year of the Lotus did. And I think the fans will enjoy the books as much as we do.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:40:16 PM)<br /> What is the status of the Osirian League. Mummy 2nd,\u00c4\u00f4s history ended with Horus frantically trying to rebuild it ,\u00c4\u00b6 yet no mention of these development in this book. Was leaving it out a design decision or were there other factors?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:41:31 PM)<br /> Partially a design factor, partially other elements.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:43:03 PM)<br /> This gets into some WW history, which isn't really germane. In short: I was involved in the game's initial design, but wasn't tapped for developer off-hand. I came on board later to do final development, and by that time much of the material was already complete. And in that material, I never saw mention of the Osirian League. So it's quite possible the writers felt it wasn't worth carrying forward.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:43:51 PM)<br /> Then again, it could've just been an oversight. It happens. (If players liked it, though, they can pull it from the previous Mummy book. Plus, if there /are/ supplements down the road, who's to say it won't crop up again?)<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:44:26 PM)<br /> How does mummy effect the world of Darkness as a whole<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:44:46 PM)<br /> It pokes a big stick in the anthill a half-dozen times.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:45:23 PM)<br /> You have what amounts to a new breed of supernatural, really something that's been around since forever (and will be into eternity), but never before amounted to much or did anything of consequence.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:46:04 PM)<br /> Now, on the heels of all these upstart mortals stalking supernatural critters, we have these mummies (who aren't your grandpa's immortals), being almost as active.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:46:41 PM)<br /> Even the oldest vampires have no precedent for this. The mumies were always somewhat a mystery to other supernaturals, and these new Amenti are even moreso.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:47:18 PM)<br /> So they're confusing the heck out of everyone, at the same time not sitting around quietly and letting the other supernaturals continue their comfy status quo.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:47:42 PM)<br /> Of course, how, exactly, that impacts things in the end depends on your own games. As always.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:48:04 PM)<br /> When the book says taht the new Spell of Life is more complete than the old Spell, in what ways does it mean?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:49:06 PM)<br /> The most notable thing is that the old Spell of Life left the mummy sterile, and his life force didn't seem quite as strong as a mortal's. The new Spell of Life restores the Amenti utterly; that is to say, a virile, energetic being.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:49:47 PM)<br /> More alive than the living, if you will.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:50:05 PM)<br /> I missed the first half of this chat, so it could have already been asked- but what's the power level of a &quot;new&quot; mummy like compared to the &quot;old&quot; ones.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:50:32 PM)<br /> Good question. We tried to make the power levels roughly equivalent.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:50:58 PM)<br /> Equivalent to other WOD games I think is what he means there <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/image/png;base64,R0lGODlhGQAZAHcAMSH  ZAP ZM/ ZZv Zmf ZzP Z///MAP/MM//MZv/Mmf/MzP/M////AP//M///Zv//mf//zP///wECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwECAwj/AAEIHChwBYAVVgwSXMjwicA8gEiRypOHoUU9VSQ6U0XNmbNRpKroUbjwSZU8qpx1XOnR2cQqDhfq eOxmkpnNlemzKOH4IoqgDxSUwWI41A9LT1WVGglT82NT2oCsjJq5ShneawIzHiTGikrRkPebBnyIKBROYdGxfkHbE6Po3oCcNr1q1FVVYy2RJbHIalUHXOS0rlxZbOPpFY8AdSRFMeuKqnp1JinygpSHldwfPu2o6oViA06VaWHsWTILadi7gvg7FBAeVjK/qPnalyDXF blswbkB7Mx8o dNaM2ijYsCcit42sysCfdDditGJlOuZRoyr61OP0KlxnqT5 JeQrl6DJPKSQJW0JsnJMixltj 8k3OJAh9wpTtRu32JCgf9ZFBAAOw==\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:51:53 PM)<br /> The Hekau are revamped, with effort made to enhance play balance and versatility. So they're a pretty potent opponent to any other supernatural, without being able to run roughshod over everyone.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:52:50 PM)<br /> A mummy with sufficient ability in Amulets, Alchemy, Effigy and the like who takes the time to create a bunch of amulets and potions and statue minions, could really clean house if he wanted to.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:53:20 PM)<br /> But they take damage just like mortals do, so it doesn't pay to get overconfident. (Although the Amenti will come back to life if things go bad...)<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:54:24 PM)<br /> How does the population of the new mummies compare to the one of th old ones? Are they more numerous?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:54:47 PM)<br /> They are noticeably more numerous. That's one of the things that has vampires and such in a tizzy.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:56:04 PM)<br /> Can Mummies return from death faster than in previous editions? Speaking from experience, if your Mummy got ganked, it was a major pain in downtime.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:57:13 PM)<br /> Pretty much. We reconfigured how some of the Traits work, including Ba. That Trait now dictates how quickly the mummy's spirit can re-inhabit its body.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:57:47 PM)<br /> With no Ba rating, the mummy must wait a year between cycles. With Ba 5, the mummy can pop back up in a day.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 7:58:15 PM)<br /> (It's a Background, by the way; hence the 0 to 5 rating.)<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 7:59:23 PM)<br /> Is there any way to put a mummy down for good? Or are you pretty much screwed in the long run if you get a bunch as an enemy?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:00:36 PM)<br /> You're kinda screwed. Mention's made of some ceremony that destroys a mummy so utterly its as if he never existed (this is a carry over from previous Mummy editions, as some of you may know).<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:01:09 PM)<br /> Also, it's mentioned that if a mummy's spirit is successfully destroyed, that's it for him. By no means an easy thing to do, though.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:01:37 PM)<br /> This is another thing that has other supernaturals so nervous at the moment, of course.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:02:01 PM)<br /> (Especially those eternal schemers, vampires, who are used to simply outlasting their enemies.)<br /> <br /> <b>Random Comment </b>(21-Mar-01 8:02:36 PM)<br /> But the mummy came back, the very next day...<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:03:06 PM)<br /> I'm not sure if this question has been asked, but what will we see, if anything, in the way of non-Egyptian mummies?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:03:46 PM)<br /> Yes indeedy. M:tR has an Appendix that talks about that very thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:04:46 PM)<br /> Specifically, it mentions the Mesoamerican mummies, referred to in general as the Capacocha; and Asian mummies, labeled the Wu T'ian. (Not to be confused with the Wu-Tang, of course.)<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:05:11 PM)<br /> This information includes special powers available solely to those groups, too.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:05:30 PM)<br /> Aside from the Shemsu-Heru's edicts laid down by Horus, the Children of Osiris, Cult of Isis and others make no mention of rules that restrict the Amenti from revealing their existance or the existance of other supernaturals to the mortal population. While some of the Amenti would naturally asume a very low profile too avoid their Foes' attention, are there pressure on the reborn not to let the cat out of the bag to rally Humanity to the Banner of Osiris?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:07:07 PM)<br /> There isn't much stated explicitly about that, no. (I'm of the opinion that slapping on too much of those kinds of strictures gets a little silly; if someone /really/ wants their character to tell the world &quot;hey, I'm a mummy!&quot; no amount of words in the book is going to stop them.) But...<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:08:42 PM)<br /> Thinking practically, it's probably not the best idea. A mummy is immortal, but he can be destroyed. By revealing himself to the world, he's painting a big target on his forehead for any and all supernatural (and mortal) enemies to come after him. Sooner or later, a dedicated foe will find a way to get to him and take him out. And even if he's not permanently destroyed, getting knocked back to death every time he reinhabits his body is a pretty effective way to stop him from accomplishing anything.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:09:40 PM)<br /> Then there's the whole &quot;what would humanity do?&quot; angle. With the way technology is today, a mummy presenting himself as an immortal being would be regarded with skepticism (to say the least). Even those who see him die and be reborn in person wouldn't necessarily be inclined to believe him.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:09:58 PM)<br /> (Except for zealots and fringe whackjobs, who don't really help with the whole credibility angle.)<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:10:33 PM)<br /> That topic can go down a road into an hours-long discussion of the pros and cons of revealing one's true nature, though, so I'll just stop there.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:10:46 PM)<br /> Alright folks, we have only about 15 more minutes with Andrew Bates. Let's get out your best questions while you got him here.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:11:03 PM)<br /> Do you have a favorite Amenti faction?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:12:18 PM)<br /> I must say I like them all a lot -- something I could never say about the groups in other WoD games (even in Trinity's Aptitude division). But I guess my favorite are the Kher-Minu, the Tomb Watchers.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:12:44 PM)<br /> I like the Amulets Hekau, which is their primary magic path, and the main mummy character in the Scarab trilogy I'm writing is one of their group.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:13:14 PM)<br /> (I'd picked it before I'd settled on a favorite, and in writing him, I just came to enjoy the character and the types of things such faction members can do.)<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:13:29 PM)<br /> I'm a bit confused about the differences between the mummy &quot;types&quot; &amp; how a tem-akh picks a mortal. Take an immoral guy climbing the corporate ladder ... seems like he could be a candidate for the Kher-minu (workaholic), the Mesektet (deceptive), or the Sakhmu (selfish). Similarly meek folks could end up Khri-habi or Sefekhi. Can you give a bit of guidance on what kinds of things most influence a tem-akh when picking a mortal partner?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:14:41 PM)<br /> The latitude you mention is intentional. There are parameters, as mention in what the tem-akh look for, but we wanted to leave some wiggle room in case a player prefers a certain Amenti over another.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:14:45 PM)<br /> That being said...<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:15:57 PM)<br /> (For those of you who haven't read the book yet, a tem-akh, or &quot;completing spirit&quot;, is an ancient Egyptian spirit fragment. It searches for a living person who's about to die, looking for a soul that is weakest in what it's strongest.)<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:17:01 PM)<br /> Just because a person is weakest in a particular personality angle doesn't mean he doesn't have other flaws, though. So say this corporate ladder guy is a deceptive, selfish workaholic. He's not likely all of these things equally. Is he more deceptive than selfish, or is he a workaholic above all else?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:17:49 PM)<br /> You can use those guidelines to decide which tem-akh would be most suitable. Alternatively, you can say, &quot;I like the Mesektet Amenti the best, so I'm gonna have his deceptive bit be his greatest flaw.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:18:09 PM)<br /> Whatever works best for you in the character you want to create.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:18:47 PM)<br /> Will mummy's have some sort of past life background or the like representing their memmory of their past<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:18:56 PM)<br /> (No, that's not a cop-out, in case anyone's wondering. I'm of the opinion that you should have a fairly wide range of choices in what you can play, rather than being steered down a narrow path. But anyway...)<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:19:29 PM)<br /> Yes, there's the Background called Memory.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:19:57 PM)<br /> If you don't put any points in that, your character is mostly his modern spirit; the more points you put in, the more your character can remember his First Life.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:20:36 PM)<br /> Can you describe the Year of the Scarab Novel of Mummy that is going to be released soon?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:21:46 PM)<br /> It's a trilogy, actually. The first novel, Heralds of the Storm (released in April, I think), draws a band of hunters into a plot to capture an ancient artifact hidden in Chicago, and the efforts of a certain nasty supernatural fellow who hopes to learn the secret of the Spell of LIfe.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:22:35 PM)<br /> The second novel, Lay Down With Lions, puts vampires on the scene, who've been wondering just what the heck's up with these hunters and now these pesky mummies. (It also features Beckett of Vampire fame;<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:23:34 PM)<br /> the trilogy also includes Bookworm/Jake and Cabbie/Lupe from Hunter and Carpenter from Hunter/Wraith, with cameos by some Chicago primogen, Horus, and a few other folks.<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:24:09 PM)<br /> The third book involves a race to stop the bad guy with all sorts of cool set pieces in Egypt. (I haven't written that yet, though, so don't know exactly what happens...)<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:24:34 PM)<br /> (The main mummy character, Nicholas Sforza, has a name some might find familiar, but he's a fresh character on the scene.)<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:25:33 PM)<br /> were do the vampire clan setites play into the mummy concept?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:26:25 PM)<br /> The Setites are the primary enemies of the mummies. As Set's followers, they're top on the list for retribution. Although the mummies are happy to take the fight to vampires in general, of course.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:28:57 PM)<br /> approx. how many Shemsu Heru survived the last Maelstrom?<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:29:11 PM)<br /> Cop-out answer: as many as you want.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:29:29 PM)<br /> Only one more question folks, just one more, make it a good one<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:29:50 PM)<br /> We left that open for folks to tweak in their games as they saw fit.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:30:27 PM)<br /> Most mummies think the Imkhu are all that remains of the original Shemsu-heru, but they could be wrong...<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:30:57 PM)<br /> Far be it from the World of Darkness to provide a straight answer, right?<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:31:23 PM)<br /> Okay folks, I think that's about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:31:30 PM)<br /> Hmm, am I forgetting anything?<br /> <br /> <b>JohnP. (ID=38)</b> (21-Mar-01 8:31:37 PM)<br /> prizes!<br /> <br /> <b>He_Hate_Me (ID=57)</b> (21-Mar-01 8:31:38 PM)<br /> PRIZES!!!<br /> <br /> <b>Andrew Bates</b> (21-Mar-01 8:31:44 PM)<br /> Heh.<br /> <br /> <b>Tanith (ID=40)</b> (21-Mar-01 8:31:47 PM)<br /> Free stuff!<br /> <br /> <b>Traelik'han (ID=28)</b> (21-Mar-01 8:31:47 PM)<br /> women!<br /> <br /> <b>Moderator Conrad</b> (21-Mar-01 8:32:29 PM)<br /> Okay, let's see, I think that the first prize will be a copy of the first of the Year of the Scarab novels, Heralds of the Storm, to be shipped to the winner 